For fixed target collisions, the normal correction methods utilized by STAR end users had to be modified to take into account the differing geometry and symmetries in the events of interest. Normally, an analysis would request for embedding. Embedding is the process of creating simulated Monte Carlo tracks of a given momentum range, species set and rapidity/pseudo-rapidity range, embedding these tracks into real raw data events, and simulating response of the subsystems utilizing the GEANT model of the STAR detector, called STARSim. Embedding allows the end user to calculate efficiencies of particle detection and

