Additionally, despite our best efforts, a conclusive determination of the projectile species cannot be made. All physics results indicate a \(Au\) or very nearly \(Au\)-like projectile, but without calculations that demonstrate a relatively large and finite probability of a beam-halo \(Au\) nucleus straying from the beam line and colliding with the beam pipe material, evidence that the projectile is \(Au\) is incomplete.

