The track matching efficiency of the TOF software is determined by comparing the number of tracks found in the TPC with the number of matched hits in the TOF detector as a function of momentum (\(m_{T}-m_{0}\)). Identified particle plots of these ratios are shown in Figure 4.28. The tracks are identified through dE/dx in the TPC when the energy loss is within \(1\sigma\) of the predicted Bichsel [142] parameterization. These represent a pure particle sample and each track is then tested for a match in the TOF detector. In the figure, black markers indicate the positive particles, while magenta markers indicate negative particles. This distribution is fit with a function of the form,

